{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Getting the Job You Want"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Practical Advice"}, {"type": "position", "content": 6}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 9}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.1"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe hypothetical situations in written and spoken interactions according to work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts. "}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts. "}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Future Continuous Tense vs. The Future Perfect Tense "}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the Future Continuous tense to talk about something happening at a particular time in the future.<br/>You use the Future Perfect tense to talk about an action in the future before another action in the future. This is the past in the future. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you use the <span class=\"strong\">Future Continuous</span> tense, the action will have started before that moment but it will not have finished at that moment."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:  <br/><span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">will be working</span> at 4 p.m. tomorrow. </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "The person will start work at some point in the future and be working at 4 p.m. It is not clear when the person will stop working. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "The structure of the Future Continuous is: <br/>Subject + <span class=\"italic\">will</span> + <span class=\"italic\">be</span> + verb <span class=\"italic\">-ing</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">By this time tomorrow, we <span class=\"strong\">will be getting on</span> a plane heading on our vacation. </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can sometimes think of the <span class=\"strong\">Future Perfect</span> tense like the Present Perfect tense, but instead of your viewpoint being in the present, it is in the future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example: <br/> <span class=\"italic\">You can call me at work at 8 a.m. I <span class=\"strong\">will have arrived</span> at the office by 8.  <br/>The train will leave the station at 9 a.m. You will arrive at the station at 9:15 a.m. When you arrive, the train <span class=\"strong\">will have left</span>.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "The structure of the Future Perfect tense is: <br/>Subject + <span class=\"italic\">will </span>+ (<span class=\"italic\">not</span>) <span class=\"italic\">have </span>+ past participle"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">By this time tomorrow <span class=\"strong\">we will have finished</span> our project.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": " *Notice the position of <span class=\"italic\">not</span>. It comes between <span class=\"italic\">will</span> and <span class=\"italic\">have</span>."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Do you think we will have it finished by 9:00 p.m. tonight ?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Will we be working on it all night?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "By this time tomorrow we will have finished our project and we will be getting on a plane heading on our vacation. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Mike will have done all his work by 5:00 p.m."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I think we'll have put it to bed before that even. I think we'll have it ready by 6:00, maybe 7 ... at the max."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I will be doing some research on Corbin. "}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Tag Questions"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use tag questions to ask for clarification and confirmation."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Question tags are short questions at the end of statements."}, {"type": "text", "content": "They are mainly used in speech when we want to:<ul><li><span class=\"strong\">clarify/confirm whether something is true or not true</span>, or</li><li><span class=\"strong\">to encourage a reply</span> from the person we are speaking to.</li></ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ol><li value=\"1\">A <span class=\"strong\">positive</span> statement is followed by a <span class=\"strong\">negative</span> question tag.<br/> Use this when you think the other person will agree by saying \u2018yes' <span class=\"italic\"><ul><li>You <span class=\"strong\">were</span> taken by surprise, <span class=\"strong\">weren't you?</span></li> <li>You <span class=\"strong\">are</span> Canadian, <span class=\"strong\">aren't</span> you?</li> <li>She <span class=\"strong\">has</span> a brother, <span class=\"strong\">doesn't</span> she?</li> <li>He <span class=\"strong\">can</span> speak English, <span class=\"strong\">can't</span> he?</li></ul></span></li></ol>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ol><li value=\"2\">A <span class=\"strong\">negative</span> statement is followed by a <span class=\"strong\">positive</span> question tag.<br/> Use this when you think the other person will agree by saying \u2018no'  <span class=\"italic\"><ul><li>You <span class=\"strong\">weren't</span> taken by surprise, <span class=\"strong\">were you? </span></li> <li>You <span class=\"strong\">aren't</span> Canadian, <span class=\"strong\">are</span> you?</li> <li>She <span class=\"strong\">doesn't</span> have a brother, <span class=\"strong\">does</span> she?</li> <li>He <span class=\"strong\">can't</span> speak English, <span class=\"strong\">can</span> he?</li></ul></span> </li></ol>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "If the main verb is <span class=\"italic\">to be</span> or a <span class=\"strong\">modal verb</span>, the tag will be the same. <br/>For <span class=\"strong\">all other main verbs</span>, use the tag <span class=\"italic\">do</span>/<span class=\"italic\">does </span>or <span class=\"italic\">did</span>/<span class=\"italic\">didn't</span>. <br/>Look at the examples in the chart."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":11,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Main Verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Tag\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Main Verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Tag\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He is/was\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" isn't/wasn't he?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" She has/had\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" doesn't/didn't she?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" You are\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" aren't you?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" You have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" don't you?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" He can\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" can't he?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" He likes\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" doesn't he?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" We could\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" couldn't we?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" You like\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" don't you?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" You will\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" won't you?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" You liked\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" didn't you?\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I think we met at Jack's house, didn't we?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Hey ... I know you, don't I?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "We were all at Melrose bar, weren't we?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "You work at Corbin Development, don't you?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Sure, you will be heading this way, won't you? "}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Create an elevator pitch with a partner."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Think of a situation when you would need to make an elevator pitch."}, {"type": "text", "content": "An elevator pitch is a brief, persuasive speech that you use to spark interest."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can create interest in a project, idea, or product or in yourself. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "A good elevator pitch is 20 to 30 seconds, but make yours 1 minute."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Role play with a partner. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Try to talk about what you will be doing or what you will have done in your pitch. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you are ready change partners."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I collaborate with a partner."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I create an elevator pitch dialogue."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I use will be doing or what I will have done to talk about future plans."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I act out and perform my dialogue."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn9le09ob06re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to over hear"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to hear a conversation without the speaker intention or notice"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:I couldn't help but overhear your conversation."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le09ob06aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "put to bed"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to complete work on something and send it on to the next step in production"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I think we'll have put it to bed before that even."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le09ob06aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "max"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "maximum"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I think we'll have it ready by 6:00, maybe 7 \u2026 at the max."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le09ob06aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "proposal"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the act of proposing"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:We are finishing up a development proposal for the city planners. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le09ob06aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "neck of the woods"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "area of the country "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:What are you doing in this neck of the woods? "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le09ob06aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to head"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to go at the head or at the front  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You will be heading this way, won't you?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le09ob06aud06"}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "type": "WLC", "questions": [], "img_path": "", "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about emotions, opinions and behavior in a work situation. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about what I will be doing or what I will have done. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can ask for clarification and ask for someone's opinion. "}, {"typ